// The Open Universe codex - read in-game from the Codex tab. This is a classic
// documents AMD: `# [Title](key)` headings are the table-of-contents entries; the
// prose (with bare ## / ### markdown headings) is rendered as the content. Unlike
// the universe data files, this is parsed by the default documents reader, so bare
// headings here are formatting, not sections.

# [Welcome, Captain](intro)
You command a ship on an open frontier - a galaxy you explore one jump at a time,
the same seed always regenerating the same stars.

## [The Frontier](the_frontier)
Engage the jump drive on the Navigation console to travel between systems. Each is
a pure function of the universe seed: revisit one and it is unchanged. Clans hold
territory, traders run lanes, raiders prowl the dark.

## [How the galaxy sees you](how_the_galaxy_sees_you)
The galaxy reacts to who you are, not to a scripted hero. Every clan keeps a read
on your conduct across seven spectrums - honest/liar, fearsome/cowardly, and so on.
Do a clan's work and it warms to you; cross it and it remembers.

# [The Clans](clans)
Six powers divide the frontier. Two are foes by default; the rest are negotiable.

## [Iron Concord](iron_concord)
Disciplined and territorial military. Respects strength and straight dealing -
honor a deal and the Concord remembers, break one and they remember longer.

## [Verdant Pact](verdant_pact)
Green-world traders and farmers. Quick to deal, slow to fight; pay them in kindness
and they pay you back in goods.

## [Free Holders](free_holders)
Independent settlers scratching a living from the drift. Self-reliant and plain-
spoken; they value a captain who gets things done.

## [Mercury Guild](mercury_guild)
Brokers of muscle and cargo - loyal to the contract, not the cause. Coin and a
fearsome reputation open their doors.

## [Ashfang Raiders](foe)
Opportunist pirates who prey on the lanes. They respect violence and despise the
weak; only the dangerous bargain with them. Captain Vex Karr, the Ash-Captain,
runs the Ashfang home in the Ashen Reach and collects grudges like trophies.

## [Hollow Choir](foe)
A secretive cult chasing forbidden knowledge in the deep dark. Honeyed words hide
sharp intent; trust them at your peril.

# [Reputation & Diplomacy](reputation)
Reputation is per-captain - it follows you across ships. Diplomacy is side-wide -
whether your fleets are at war. They interact: earn a foe clan's respect and you
can buy a ceasefire, or in time an alliance.

## [Standing](standing)
A clan's standing with you is your reputation weighted by what that clan values.
High standing unlocks better jobs and cheaper ceasefires; low standing with a
clan's captains can turn them into personal rivals.

# [The Regions](regions)
The frontier is not uniform. Named regions carry their own character - and their
own dangers.

## [The Ashen Reach](the_ashen_reach)
Ashfang raider country off the system (8, -5). A warzone: enemy systems crowd the
lanes and mines lace the dark. Red skies, worse intentions.

## [The Verdant Belt](the_verdant_belt)
The Verdant Pact's trade lanes around (-5, 3). A haven: no raiders, ports
everywhere. Calm, open, prosperous.
